<figure class="case-lead-image"><img src="/img/portfolio/threshold-uk-housing-failure-title-slide.webp" width="2400" height="1350" alt="Threshold presentation title slide reading UK Housing Failure."></figure>

<section class="case-summary">
  <div><p class="eyebrow">The problem</p><h2>Informing an audience was not enough. The material needed to build a case.</h2></div>
  <div class="prose"><p>This self-initiated example explores advocacy communication around housing. The source material contains competing explanations, long-term data and policy choices. The challenge is to establish a position without losing the evidence behind it.</p><p>The sequence moves from problem framing, through a memorable comparison and supporting data, towards a practical alternative.</p></div>
</section>

<section class="decision-band"><span>01</span><div><p class="eyebrow">The decision</p><h2>Make the scale of the failure visible before explaining its causes.</h2></div></section>

<section class="case-gallery" data-gallery>
  <figure class="gallery-wide"><img src="/img/portfolio/threshold-social-housing-shortfall-statistic.webp" width="2400" height="1350" loading="lazy" alt="Threshold slide showing a shortfall of 1.34 million social homes since 1980."><figcaption><strong>Magnitude before detail.</strong> One defining number establishes the scale of the shortfall before the argument moves into causes.</figcaption></figure>
  <figure><img src="/img/portfolio/threshold-housing-supply-problem-framing-slide.webp" width="2400" height="1350" loading="lazy" alt="Threshold slide framing the relationship between housing supply, delivery and commercial incentives."><figcaption><strong>Frame the debate.</strong> A short sequence connects supply constraints, delivery and commercial incentives.</figcaption></figure>
  <figure><img src="/img/portfolio/threshold-permissions-homes-completed-chart.webp" width="2400" height="1350" loading="lazy" alt="Threshold chart comparing planning permissions with homes completed."><figcaption><strong>Test the assumption.</strong> The permissions and completions gap is made visible and annotated.</figcaption></figure>
  <figure><img src="/img/portfolio/threshold-council-housebuilding-policy-timeline.webp" width="2400" height="1350" loading="lazy" alt="Threshold timeline connecting the decline in council housebuilding with policy decisions."><figcaption><strong>Explain the long view.</strong> The timeline links the collapse in council housebuilding to policy decisions.</figcaption></figure>
  <figure><img src="/img/portfolio/threshold-regional-housing-pressure-comparison.webp" width="2400" height="1350" loading="lazy" alt="Threshold slide comparing housing pressures across UK regions."><figcaption><strong>Add necessary depth.</strong> Regional comparison prevents a national average from hiding local differences.</figcaption></figure>
  <figure><img src="/img/portfolio/threshold-three-housing-policy-changes.webp" width="2400" height="1350" loading="lazy" alt="Threshold slide presenting three changes that would improve UK housing delivery."><figcaption><strong>Lead with a memorable proposition.</strong> Three policy priorities give the argument a concise destination.</figcaption></figure>
  <figure><img src="/img/portfolio/threshold-alternative-development-model-diagram.webp" width="2400" height="1350" loading="lazy" alt="Threshold diagram showing an alternative model for housing development."><figcaption><strong>Move from diagnosis to action.</strong> The final framework gives the audience a model to discuss.</figcaption></figure>
</section>

<section class="case-outcome"><div><p class="eyebrow">The practical output</p><h2>A presentation argument with editable charts, diagrams and a clear sequence.</h2></div><p>This is self-initiated work, created to demonstrate our method rather than represent a client engagement. It shows how our <a href="/services/presentation-design/">presentation design</a> moves from evidence and structure to a finished advocacy presentation.</p></section>

